; Test: Defeater blocked by superiority
; Coverage: rule superior to defeater can still prove its conclusion

; r1 supports q, d1 is a defeater for ~q.
; With r1 > d1, the defeater is overcome.
(given p)
(normally r1 p q)
(except d1 p (not q))
(prefer r1 d1)

; r1 > d1, so q is provable despite the defeater
; EXPECT: +D p
; EXPECT: +d p
; EXPECT: +d q

; Without superiority, defeater blocks:
(given m)
(normally r2 m w)
(except d2 m (not w))

; No prefer => defeater blocks both w and ~w
; EXPECT: +D m
; EXPECT: +d m
; EXPECT: -d w
; EXPECT: -d ~w
